WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.787
About three thousand six hundred people live in the Falklands today.

00:00:04.887 --> 00:00:09.705
Life divides between Stanley, the capital, and Camp, from the Spanish word campo:

00:00:09.705 --> 00:00:14.047
the countryside of sheep farms linked by rough tracks and small aircraft.

00:00:15.147 --> 00:00:17.585
Since a fishing zone was declared in 1986,

00:00:17.585 --> 00:00:22.577
licences for squid fishing have transformed a wool economy into one of the richest per

00:00:22.577 --> 00:00:23.796
person in the region.

00:00:23.796 --> 00:00:27.802
The Falklands are a clear case of loyalty to a former imperial power,

00:00:27.802 --> 00:00:31.749
and of how a contested history shapes which island stories get told.
